msgid "If a state cookie is present then a `state` query parameter must also be present and both the state cookie name suffix and state cookie value have to match the value of the `state` query parameter when the redirect path matches the current path. However, if multiple authentications are attempted from the same browser, for example, from the different browser tabs, then the currently available state cookie may represent the authentication flow initiated from another tab and not related to the current request. Disable this property to permit only a single authorization code flow in the same browser."
